{"code":"33-2011.00","title":"Firefighters","description":"Control and extinguish fires or respond to emergency situations where life, property, or the environment is at risk. Duties may include fire prevention, emergency medical service, hazardous material response, search and rescue, and disaster assistance.","jobZone":2,"kinds":{"R":{"score":6.49,"share":0.3763},"I":{"score":2.92,"share":0.1316},"A":{"score":1.31,"share":0.0212},"S":{"score":3.39,"share":0.1638},"E":{"score":3.01,"share":0.1378},"C":{"score":3.47,"share":0.1693}},"highPoints":["R"],"tasks":[{"id":22961,"text":"Rescue survivors from burning buildings, accident sites, and water hazards.","core":true,"importance":4.47,"relevance":100,"frequency":2.2},{"id":22962,"text":"Dress with equipment such as fire-resistant clothing and breathing apparatus.","core":true,"importance":4.37,"relevance":100,"frequency":3.41},{"id":22987,"text":"Administer first aid and cardiopulmonary resuscitation to injured persons or provide emergency medical care such as basic or advanced life support.","core":true,"importance":4.37,"relevance":96.13,"frequency":3.22},{"id":22964,"text":"Move toward the source of a fire, using knowledge of types of fires, construction design, building materials, and physical layout of properties.","core":true,"importance":4.31,"relevance":97.48,"frequency":2.87},{"id":22967,"text":"Drive and operate fire fighting vehicles and equipment.","core":true,"importance":4.3,"relevance":97.48,"frequency":3.74},{"id":22965,"text":"Respond to fire alarms and other calls for assistance, such as automobile and industrial accidents.","core":true,"importance":4.28,"relevance":100,"frequency":3.78},{"id":22989,"text":"Search to locate fire survivors.","core":true,"importance":4.27,"relevance":93.75,"frequency":1.98},{"id":22988,"text":"Operate pumps connected to high-pressure hoses.","core":true,"importance":4.24,"relevance":95.54,"frequency":3.18},{"id":22971,"text":"Maintain contact with fire dispatchers at all times to notify them of the need for additional firefighters and supplies, or to detail any difficulties encountered.","core":true,"importance":4.23,"relevance":97.48,"frequency":3.61},{"id":22986,"text":"Extinguish flames and embers to suppress fires, using shovels or engine- or hand-driven water or chemical pumps.","core":true,"importance":4.22,"relevance":97.38,"frequency":2.46},{"id":22976,"text":"Maintain knowledge of current firefighting practices by participating in drills and by attending seminars, conventions, and conferences.","core":true,"importance":4.18,"relevance":99.99,"frequency":3.24},{"id":22970,"text":"Select and attach hose nozzles, depending on fire type, and direct streams of water or chemicals onto fires.","core":true,"importance":4.17,"relevance":97.38,"frequency":2.72},{"id":22972,"text":"Collaborate with other firefighters as a member of a firefighting crew.","core":true,"importance":4.13,"relevance":97.48,"frequency":3.31},{"id":22966,"text":"Create openings in buildings for ventilation or entrance, using axes, chisels, crowbars, electric saws, or core cutters.","core":true,"importance":4.12,"relevance":97.38,"frequency":2.28},{"id":22969,"text":"Position and climb ladders to gain access to upper levels of buildings, or to rescue individuals from burning structures.","core":true,"importance":4.12,"relevance":97.38,"frequency":2.26},{"id":22990,"text":"Train new employees to control and suppress fires.","core":true,"importance":4.12,"relevance":89.43,"frequency":2.95},{"id":22975,"text":"Participate in fire drills and demonstrations of fire fighting techniques.","core":true,"importance":4.11,"relevance":97.48,"frequency":3.22},{"id":22963,"text":"Assess fires and situations and report conditions to superiors to receive instructions, using two-way radios.","core":true,"importance":4.1,"relevance":100,"frequency":2.9},{"id":22968,"text":"Inspect fire sites after flames have been extinguished to ensure that there is no further danger.","core":true,"importance":4.05,"relevance":90.85,"frequency":2.46},{"id":22973,"text":"Patrol burned areas after fires to locate and eliminate hot spots that may restart fires.","core":true,"importance":4.05,"relevance":100,"frequency":2.39},{"id":22985,"text":"Take action to contain any hazardous chemicals that could catch fire, leak, or spill.","core":true,"importance":4.05,"relevance":96.86,"frequency":2.16},{"id":22977,"text":"Prepare written reports that detail specifics of fire incidents.","core":true,"importance":4.02,"relevance":92.31,"frequency":2.73},{"id":22979,"text":"Protect property from water and smoke, using waterproof salvage covers, smoke ejectors, and deodorants.","core":true,"importance":4,"relevance":88.04,"frequency":2.16},{"id":22984,"text":"Inspect buildings for fire hazards and compliance with fire prevention ordinances, testing and checking smoke alarms and fire suppression equipment as necessary.","core":true,"importance":3.96,"relevance":70.16,"frequency":2.36},{"id":22974,"text":"Collaborate with police to respond to accidents, disasters, and arson investigation calls.","core":true,"importance":3.94,"relevance":100,"frequency":3.26},{"id":22981,"text":"Salvage property by removing broken glass, pumping out water, and ventilating buildings to remove smoke.","core":true,"importance":3.93,"relevance":94.34,"frequency":2.56},{"id":22982,"text":"Orient self in relation to fire, using compass and map, and collect supplies and equipment dropped by parachute.","core":false,"importance":3.89,"relevance":47.5,"frequency":2.12},{"id":22980,"text":"Inform and educate the public on fire prevention.","core":true,"importance":3.87,"relevance":90.14,"frequency":2.05},{"id":22983,"text":"Clean and maintain fire stations and fire fighting equipment and apparatus.","core":true,"importance":3.87,"relevance":100,"frequency":3.47},{"id":22978,"text":"Participate in physical training activities to maintain a high level of physical fitness.","core":true,"importanc